"**Scene: In the Thriller Film \"Shadows of Silence\"**\n\n**INT. ABANDONED WAREHOUSE - NIGHT**\n\nA dim, flickering overhead light casts long shadows across the vast, dusty space. Sounds of distant sirens echo in the background. We see *JANE*, mid-30s, impeccably dressed in a business suit, sitting at an old, worn-out table. Across from her is *MARK*, late 40s, visibly tense, hands gripping the edge of his chair.\n\n*Jane leans in, her voice smooth yet steely, as she carefully places a thick envelope on the table between them.*\n\n**JANE**  \n(voice dripping with faux concern)  \nMark, I understand that you've been under a lot of pressure lately. You know how it is—business isn't easy. I'm sure there are times when you wish you could just walk away without a care.\n\n*Mark shifts uncomfortably, his eyes darting to the envelope before returning to Jane’s probing gaze.*\n\n**JANE**  \n(smiling softly)  \nAnd I’m sure there’s a lot you’re carrying right now that would make life a whole lot simpler. A clean slate, so to speak. Just one more transaction, and you can have it.  \n\n*Jane pauses, watching Mark closely, then leans back, letting the tension in the room build.*\n\n**JANE**  \n(firmly)  \nYou’re a smart man, Mark. The kind who knows when to hold 'em and when to fold 'em. This... envelope? It’s just a formality. Consider it your out.\n\n*The faint rustle of paper can be heard as the envelope is shifted on the table. Mark takes a deep breath, realizing the gravity of the situation.*\n\n**MARK**  \n(voice trembling)  \nWhat’s in there? And what happens if I—\n\n**JANE**  \n(cutting him off with a reassuring smile)  \nOh, let’s not get ahead of ourselves. Let’s think of this as insurance. A way to protect what matters most to you. Let’s just get this done, alright?\n\n*Jane’s eyes lock onto Mark’s, leaving an unspoken threat hanging in the air. He nods slowly, the weight of compliance settling on his shoulders.*\n\n**MARK**  \nAlright. What do you need from me?\n\n**JANE**  \n(thoughtfully)  \nJust make sure it’s done the right way, and everyone walks away happy. I trust you’ll handle it"
