"**Title: Silent Echoes**\n\n**INT. A DIMLY LIT STUDY ROOM - NIGHT**\n\nThe room is cloaked in shadows, illuminated only by the flickering flame of a single candle casting a gentle glow over a worn-out desk. Papers, in disarray, are scattered across the surface. A telephone sits idly on the corner of the desk. The quiet ticking of an antique clock is the only sound that breaches the silence.\n\n**JAMES**, mid-30s, disheveled and clearly distraught, slumps into the wooden chair, his eyes heavy with exhaustion. In his hands, he clutches a crumpled piece of paper that he now unfolds with trembling fingers. \n\n**CLOSE UP** on the paper reveals it to be a list, filled with meticulous, hurried scrawls. He reads it, his voice barely a whisper, betraying a haunting hopelessness.\n\n**JAMES**\n(reading aloud, almost to himself)\nGather your thoughts, close your eyes for a moment. Contemplate the weight of your burdens. \n\nHe pauses, the gravity of his situation momentarily resting on his shoulders. He flicks his gaze to a photo of a smiling woman — his wife — wedged between two of the books on the shelf. Her memory seems to beckon him with both comfort and torment.\n\n**JAMES**  \nThen, write one final letter to those you cherish. Express your love, your regrets, the dreams unfulfilled. A goodbye without a trace of bitterness. \n\nHe sets down the paper and picks up a pen, pressing it to a sheet of clean paper. He scribbles down a few lines, his hand trembling yet determined. Satisfied, he folds the letter, placing it gently beside a framed photograph on the mantle above the fireplace.\n\n**JAMES**\nAnd lastly, seek solitude, where no sound can reach you but your own heartbeat. \n\nHe stands, his silhouette elongated by the candle's light, as he walks towards a window draped in heavy curtains. He draws them aside, revealing a moonlit landscape. For a brief moment, he stands in quiet contemplation, his breath visible in the chilled air.\n\nAs he turns away, the scene shifts to a close-up of the list on the desk, the camera slowly panning over each item as the door to the room creaks open. A **GENTLE FINGER** touches the list, setting it aside before a kind face peers inside. \n\n**ANNA**, late 20s"
